D12 is complete. The final report is at `collab/1791284000000-compiler-engineer-ucf-d12-reader.findings.md`.

## Summary

**What was built** — the holder-side recorded reader and replay, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/reader.cljc` plus its test file, nothing else. **`engine.cljc` needed no addition**: all six public applies the reader owes (`apply-mint`, `-observation`, `-next`, `-ffi-read`, `-link-cursor`, `-link-read`) already existed from D4–D6.

**The seam** mirrors the writer's: `step` takes the composition-supplied input appender and handle observer; `settle`/`drain` consume attributed `:yin.k/input` replies; `replay` is pure (no observer at all). One observation in flight at a time, held under `:yin.k/held` in the four retained states; sources live inside `:yin.k/name` with the `:cursor` origin form (residual 1) and no cell ids, host cursors, or sealed references anywhere. Mints precede reads in `:seq` order; reads defer to pending closes; a prefix with no exact frontier fails closed, never as empty.

