Red evidence is in the report: the test-first load failure, then two genuine defect rounds — a nil read handle in the observer, and `update-in` with the root's empty assoc path (which assoc's under a nil key, silently corrupting every held-state transition).

**Two judgment calls worth your eye**: the row-5 divergent leg is test-authored (an honest driver can't reach a same-id divergent write — the authority answers `:input-conflict` at the recorded k first), and the input-conflict fixture's pre-record carries its own opaque request id, since under one lease an earlier same-id reply would legitimately ack a held request by the writer's own correlation rules. kondo/cljstyle were sandbox-blocked directly and ran through spawned processes — noted in the report. No git writes were made.
